},{"name":"maxIterations","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The matrix–vector products each Lanczos run may spend; nil for 20,000 +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"20√n.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","anchor":"return-value","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The eigenpairs, in order from that end of the spectrum."}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization and locking on σI − M (σ","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Gershgorin’s bound), from a fixed start vector; once k pairs are found, a run on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"complement of their vectors checks that no copy of a multiple eigenvalue was missed. A Ritz","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pair is accepted when its residual is at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" · max(|λ|, s\/1000), s Gershgorin’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bound on the spectrum; the vectors are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, whose values are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returned. The dense solver below 64 vertices, or when k is a third of them or more.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"10) for the basis.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest"},{"text":" is in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},